hypotheses.statement:
On a fixed partition with $w_i=\zeta_{i+1}-\zeta_i$, the first variations along every feasible line segment of step paths are $$\begin{aligned}
\label{var:pattern-variation}
 \frac{d}{da}V_f(q+a\dot q)
 &=-\frac12\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}w_i\dot q_i\,
   \mathbb E[U_i'(Z_i)^2],\\
\label{var:field-variation}
 \frac{d}{da}\ell(h+a\dot h)
 &=-\frac12\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}w_i\dot h_i\,
   \mathbb E[U_i'(Z_i)^2].
\end{aligned}$$ The functions and chains on the right are computed at the current path. Endpoint derivatives are understood from within the segment. The squared-derivative expectations on the right are continuous on the closed finite-dimensional parameter cones. In both recursions these expectations are nonnegative and nondecreasing in $i$. In the field recursion, define $$\label{var:rho}
 \rho_h(u)=\rho_i:=\mathbb E[U_i'(Z_i)^2],
 \qquad \zeta_i<u<\zeta_{i+1}.$$ Then $0\le\rho_h\le1$, and subdivision does not change this path.

For step paths on arbitrary partitions, $$\begin{aligned}
\label{var:lipschitz}
 |V_f(p)-V_f(q)|&\le\tfrac12\|f'\|_\infty^2\|p-q\|_{L^1},\\
 |\ell(h')-\ell(h)|&\le\tfrac12\|h'-h\|_{L^1}.
\end{aligned}$$ Thus $V_f$ extends uniquely and continuously to all nondecreasing $[0,1]$-valued paths, and $\ell$ extends to all bounded nonnegative nondecreasing paths. Moreover, $$\label{var:tail-order}
 \int_s^1p(u)\,du\ge\int_s^1q(u)\,du
 \quad\hbox{for every }s\in[0,1]
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad V_f(p)\le V_f(q).$$

The entropy in Definition <a href="#def:entropy" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="def:entropy">2</a> is nonnegative, nondecreasing in pointwise path order, and satisfies $S_{\mathrm I}(0)=0$. The variational infimum is finite, and $$\label{var:step-infimum}
 \inf_q\{\alpha V_f(q)+S_{\mathrm I}(q)\}
 =\inf_{\substack{q\text{ step}\\q_{k-1}<1}}
       \{\alpha V_f(q)+S_{\mathrm I}(q)\}.$$

The functional $\ell$ is concave on nonnegative nondecreasing step paths. For any two such paths, represented on a common partition, $$\label{var:support}
 \ell(h')\le\ell(h)
      -\frac12\int_0^1(h'(u)-h(u))\rho_h(u)\,du.$$ Concavity also holds for its continuous extension to bounded nonnegative nondecreasing paths.

For every nondecreasing $[0,1]$-valued path $q$, $$\label{upper:conclusion}
 \limsup_{N\to\infty}\mathbb E p_N
 \le \alpha V_f(q)+S_{\mathrm I}(q).$$ Consequently the limit superior is bounded above by the variational infimum in Theorem <a href="#thm:main" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="thm:main">3</a>.

For each fixed $H<\infty$ there is a constant $C_H$, also depending on the fixed partition, $\alpha$, and $f$, such that $$\label{upper:variance}
 \operatorname{Var}(P_N(t,h,u))\le\frac{C_H}{N}$$ whenever $0\le t\le\alpha$, $0\le h_0\le\cdots\le
h_{k-1}\le H$, and $u\in[1,2]^N$.

For the fixed partition, $$\label{upper:field-growth}
 \ell(h)\le (\mathbb E|G|)\sqrt{h_0}+C_{\zeta}
                   -\frac12\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}w_ih_i.$$ For sufficiently large fixed $H$, every sufficiently large dimension in the violating sequence has a minimizer of <a href="#upper:objective" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="upper:objective">[upper:objective]</a> satisfying $t>0$ and $h_{k-1}<H$.

Start with any deterministic good parameter sequence, on any subsequence of dimensions. Pass to a further subsequence on which the omitted overlap array converges and the full system’s joint sampled arrays $(R_{lm},B_N(x^l,x^m),C_N(x^l))$ converge. Let $\mu$ be the omitted limit’s two-replica overlap law. The full limiting overlap array has the same law as the omitted one. There are deterministic constants $a_{\mathrm d},c$ and a deterministic nondecreasing function $a$, defined on a $\mu$-full ordered subset of $[0,1]$, such that almost surely $$\label{bulk:deterministic-covariances}
 B_{lm}=a(R_{lm})\quad(l\ne m),\qquad
 B_{ll}=a_{\mathrm d},\qquad C_l=c,
 \qquad 0\le a\le a_{\mathrm d}\le\alpha\|f'\|_\infty^2.$$ Moreover, $$\label{bulk:ibp-balance}
 c+a_{\mathrm d}=\int r\,a(r)\,\mu(dr).$$

Let $$\label{cav:untilted-base}
 G_0=G_N^v\otimes\nu_L$$ be the size-$N$ bulk Gibbs probability times the independent cavity-spin prior, *before* multiplication by $W$. There is a deterministic $\kappa_L>0$ such that $G_0(W)\ge\kappa_L$ for every realization and all sufficiently large $N$. Uniformly over all allowed $v$, $$\label{cav:finite-increment}
 \Delta_{N,L}(v)=\mathbb E\log G_0(W)+o(1).$$ The size-$(N+L)$ Gibbs expectations of any fixed bounded finite-replica spin test are likewise approximated, after the above coupling, by the measure $W\,dG_0/G_0(W)$, with disorder-averaged error $o(1)$ times the test’s bound. In particular this applies to bounded continuous functions of $R^+_{12}$ and their products with $z_1^1z_1^2$; inside such continuous tests one may also replace $R^+_{12}$ by $R_{12}$. Finally, $\Delta_{N,L}(v)\ge-C_L$ uniformly for large $N$.

If $f,g$ are bounded Borel functions with $|f|,|g|\le K$, then $$\begin{aligned}
 \big|\mathbb E p_N(f)-\mathbb E p_N(g)\big|
 &\le\alpha e^{2K}\|f-g\|_{L^1(\gamma)},\label{ext:pressure-distance}\\
 \sup_{q\text{ step}}|V_f(q)-V_g(q)|
 &\le e^{2K}\|f-g\|_{L^1(\gamma)}.\label{ext:path-distance}
\end{aligned}$$ Consequently, for each bounded Borel $f$, the pattern functional $V_f$ extends uniquely and continuously in $L^1$ from step paths to $\mathcal Q$, and the bound in <a href="#ext:path-distance" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="ext:path-distance">[ext:path-distance]</a> holds on all of $\mathcal Q$.

Suppose $f:\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$ is Borel and $$\label{ext:moments}
 \mathbb E|f(G)|+\mathbb E e^{f(G)}<\infty.$$ For $J,K>0$, let $f_{J,K}=\min\{K,\max\{-J,f\}\}$. The uniform limit $$\label{ext:unbounded-V}
 V_f=\lim_{J\to\infty}\lim_{K\to\infty}V_{f_{J,K}}
 \quad\text{on }\mathcal Q$$ exists and is continuous in $L^1$. With this definition, the variational formula <a href="#thm:formula" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="thm:formula">[thm:formula]</a> is finite and holds in expectation and in probability.

